concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-142 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "142 Simplified outline of this Part"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-142 ;
    values:originalText "• A controller of a local access line (other than a line that is part of the infrastructure of the national broadband network) must not use the line to supply an eligible service to a person other than a carrier or a service provider, if:  Schedule 2  Local access lines  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020 No. 47, 2020  (a) the line came into existence, or was upgraded, on or after the designated commencement date; and  (b) the line is used, or is proposed to be used, to supply a superfast carriage service wholly or principally to residential customers, or prospective residential customers, in Australia; and  (c) no functional separation undertaking is in force. • A controller of a telecommunications network (other than the national broadband network) must not use a local access line to supply an eligible service to a person other than a carrier or a service provider, if:  (a) the line is part of the infrastructure of the network; and  (b) the network came into existence, or was upgraded, on or after 1 January 2011, but before the designated commencement date; and  (c) the network is used, or is proposed to be used, to supply a superfast carriage service wholly or principally to residential customers, or prospective residential customers, in Australia; and  (d) no functional separation undertaking is in force." ;
    skos:definition "• A controller of a local access line (other than a line that is part of the infrastructure of the national broadband network) must not use the line to supply an eligible service to a person other than a carrier or a service provider, if:  Schedule 2  Local access lines  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020 No. 47, 2020  (a) the line came into existence, or was upgraded, on or after the designated commencement date; and  (b) the line is used, or is proposed to be used, to supply a superfast carriage service wholly or principally to residential customers, or prospective residential customers, in Australia; and  (c) no functional separation undertaking is in force. • A controller of a telecommunications network (other than the national broadband network) must not use a local access line to supply an eligible service to a person other than a carrier or a service provider, if:  (a) the line is part of the infrastructure of the network; and  (b) the network came into existence, or was upgraded, on or after 1 January 2011, but before the designated commencement date; and  (c) the network is used, or is proposed to be used, to supply a superfast carriage service wholly or principally to residential customers, or prospective residential customers, in Australia; and  (d) no functional separation undertaking is in force."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d94383665f7ca566c13fe35ba367269da5e34edda58e8839f7ddc67a56a8b4c0" ;
    cof:pageNumber "19"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Controller of a local access line must not supply an eligible service to a person other than a carrier or a service provider." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf> ;
