    cml:premiseText "(2) If a person (the first person):..." ;
    cml:conclusionText "...must not use the line..." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-2-sec-41-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "41(2) Subsections 143(2) and (3)" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) If a person (the first person):  (a) is in a position to exercise control of the network; or  (b) is an associate of a person who is in a position to exercise control of the network; the first person must not use the line, either alone or jointly with one or more other persons, to supply an eligible service unless the service is supplied to:  (c) a carrier; or  (d) a service provider.  Schedule 2  Local access lines  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020 No. 47, 2020  Note: For when a person is in a position to exercise control of a network, see section 155." ;
    cof:pageNumber "27"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-41-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "41(3) Subsections 143(2) and (3)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-41-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Subsection (2) does not apply to the use of the line if a functional separation undertaking given by the first person is in force, unless:  (a) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151W revoking the undertaking; and  (b) the revocation has not taken effect; and  (c) the line came into existence after the notice was given. Note 1: A functional separation undertaking relates to the supply of eligible services using a local access line, irrespective of when the line came into existence. Note 2: See also section 142B." ;
    skos:definition "(3) Subsection (2) does not apply to the use of the line if a functional separation undertaking given by the first person is in force, unless:  (a) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151W revoking the undertaking; and  (b) the revocation has not taken effect; and  (c) the line came into existence after the notice was given. Note 1: A functional separation undertaking relates to the supply of eligible services using a local access line, irrespective of when the line came into existence. Note 2: See also section 142B."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "dd08228a84757f3818776f55a2b813952a6c42d95f25b0f445b457a37f21f593" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-41 ;
    cof:pageNumber "27"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Functional separation undertaking exemption from subsection (2) application" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
