doc:sch-2-sec-151f-ss-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "151F(5) ACCC to accept or reject functional separation undertaking" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5) The ACCC must take all reasonable steps to ensure that a decision about the undertaking is made under subsection (2) within 3 months after receiving the undertaking.  Schedule 2  Local access lines  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020 No. 47, 2020" ;
    cof:pageNumber "55"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "151F(6) ACCC to accept or reject functional separation undertaking"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-151f-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) In calculating the 3-month period referred to in subsection (5), disregard:  (a) if:  (i) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151K in relation to the undertaking; and  (ii) no varied undertaking was given to the ACCC in response to the notice;  a day in the period specified in the notice; and  (b) if:  (i) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151K in relation to the undertaking; and  (ii) a varied undertaking was given to the ACCC in response to the notice;  a day in the period:  (iii) beginning on the day on which the notice was given; and  (iv) ending at the end of the time limit specified by the ACCC when it published the varied undertaking under section 151G; and  (c) if the ACCC has not given a notice under section 151K in relation to the undertaking—a day in the period:  (i) beginning on the day on which the ACCC published the undertaking under section 151G; and  (ii) ending at the end of the time limit specified by the ACCC when it published the undertaking under section 151G; and  (d) if the ACCC has requested further information under section 151D in relation to the undertaking—a day during any part of which the request, or any part of the request, remains unfulfilled. Extension of decision-making period" ;
    skos:definition "(6) In calculating the 3-month period referred to in subsection (5), disregard:  (a) if:  (i) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151K in relation to the undertaking; and  (ii) no varied undertaking was given to the ACCC in response to the notice;  a day in the period specified in the notice; and  (b) if:  (i) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151K in relation to the undertaking; and  (ii) a varied undertaking was given to the ACCC in response to the notice;  a day in the period:  (iii) beginning on the day on which the notice was given; and  (iv) ending at the end of the time limit specified by the ACCC when it published the varied undertaking under section 151G; and  (c) if the ACCC has not given a notice under section 151K in relation to the undertaking—a day in the period:  (i) beginning on the day on which the ACCC published the undertaking under section 151G; and  (ii) ending at the end of the time limit specified by the ACCC when it published the undertaking under section 151G; and  (d) if the ACCC has requested further information under section 151D in relation to the undertaking—a day during any part of which the request, or any part of the request, remains unfulfilled. Extension of decision-making period"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ee01588f0f0a3da9ebab387d448ac8a861e850eaf909598ea457f2c8cb2ba3c7" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f ;
    cof:pageNumber "55"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Disregard a day in the period specified in the notice when calculating the 3-month period." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
