doc:sch-2-sec-151f-ss-6 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "151F(6) ACCC to accept or reject functional separation undertaking" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(6) In calculating the 3-month period referred to in subsection (5), disregard:  (a) if:  (i) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151K in relation to the undertaking; and  (ii) no varied undertaking was given to the ACCC in response to the notice;  a day in the period specified in the notice; and  (b) if:  (i) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151K in relation to the undertaking; and  (ii) a varied undertaking was given to the ACCC in response to the notice;  a day in the period:  (iii) beginning on the day on which the notice was given; and  (iv) ending at the end of the time limit specified by the ACCC when it published the varied undertaking under section 151G; and  (c) if the ACCC has not given a notice under section 151K in relation to the undertaking—a day in the period:  (i) beginning on the day on which the ACCC published the undertaking under section 151G; and  (ii) ending at the end of the time limit specified by the ACCC when it published the undertaking under section 151G; and  (d) if the ACCC has requested further information under section 151D in relation to the undertaking—a day during any part of which the request, or any part of the request, remains unfulfilled. Extension of decision-making period" ;
    cof:pageNumber "55"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "151F(7) ACCC to accept or reject functional separation undertaking"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-151f-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) The ACCC may, by written notice given to the person or persons, extend the 3-month period referred to in subsection (5) (the initial 3-month period), so long as:  (a) the extension is for a period of not more than 3 months; and  Local access lines  Schedule 2  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (b) the notice includes a statement explaining why the ACCC has been unable to make a decision on the undertaking within the initial 3-month period." ;
    skos:definition "(7) The ACCC may, by written notice given to the person or persons, extend the 3-month period referred to in subsection (5) (the initial 3-month period), so long as:  (a) the extension is for a period of not more than 3 months; and  Local access lines  Schedule 2  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (b) the notice includes a statement explaining why the ACCC has been unable to make a decision on the undertaking within the initial 3-month period."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ba0f9b7e6fda5f23314aee4548d6f3412a1b05da3074fc85d62dff2d6df73bfe" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f ;
    cof:pageNumber "55"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "ACCC may extend initial 3-month period for functional separation undertaking by written notice." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
