concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151z a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "151Z Variation of functional separation undertaking following"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-151z ;
    values:originalText "giving of revocation notice Standard functional separation undertaking  (1) If:  (a) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151W revoking a standard functional separation undertaking; and  (b) the revocation has not taken effect; the ACCC may, by written notice given to the person who gave the undertaking, vary the undertaking.  (2) The ACCC must not vary a standard functional separation undertaking under subsection (1) unless the variation:  (a) addresses the matter or matters that constituted the grounds for the revocation of the undertaking under section 151W; and  (b) does not address any other matter. Joint functional separation undertaking  (3) If:  (a) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151W revoking a joint functional separation undertaking; and  (b) the revocation has not taken effect; the ACCC may, by written notice given to each of the persons who gave the undertaking, vary the undertaking.  (4) The ACCC must not vary a joint functional separation undertaking under subsection (3) unless the variation:  (a) addresses the matter or matters that constituted the grounds for the revocation of the undertaking under section 151W; and  (b) does not address any other matter.  Local access lines  Schedule 2  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  When variation takes effect  (5) A variation under subsection (1) or (3) takes effect at the time the notice is given." ;
    skos:definition "giving of revocation notice Standard functional separation undertaking  (1) If:  (a) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151W revoking a standard functional separation undertaking; and  (b) the revocation has not taken effect; the ACCC may, by written notice given to the person who gave the undertaking, vary the undertaking.  (2) The ACCC must not vary a standard functional separation undertaking under subsection (1) unless the variation:  (a) addresses the matter or matters that constituted the grounds for the revocation of the undertaking under section 151W; and  (b) does not address any other matter. Joint functional separation undertaking  (3) If:  (a) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151W revoking a joint functional separation undertaking; and  (b) the revocation has not taken effect; the ACCC may, by written notice given to each of the persons who gave the undertaking, vary the undertaking.  (4) The ACCC must not vary a joint functional separation undertaking under subsection (3) unless the variation:  (a) addresses the matter or matters that constituted the grounds for the revocation of the undertaking under section 151W; and  (b) does not address any other matter.  Local access lines  Schedule 2  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  When variation takes effect  (5) A variation under subsection (1) or (3) takes effect at the time the notice is given."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "647f92746b00569c3aa7ea3a42b4b5ef66d44a91df45f493a792a3b03b2f5d6f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "74"^^xsd:integer ;
