doc:sch-2-sec-151zf-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "151ZF(3) Eligible services to be supplied on a non-discriminatory basis" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) Examples of grounds for believing as mentioned in subsection (2) include:  (a) evidence that the wholesale customer or prospective wholesale customer is not creditworthy; and  (b) repeated failures by the wholesale customer or prospective wholesale customer to comply with the terms and conditions on which the person supplied eligible services (whether or not using the line). No discrimination by a person in favour of itself" ;
    cof:pageNumber "80"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zf-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "151ZF(4) Eligible services to be supplied on a non-discriminatory basis"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-151zf-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If:  (a) a person supplies, or proposes to supply, an eligible service using a local access line:  (i) to itself; and  (ii) to its wholesale customers or prospective wholesale customers; and  (b) any of the following conditions is satisfied:  (i) section 142C applies to the line;  (ii) section 143 applies to the line;  (iii) neither section 142C nor section 143 applies to the line, and there is in force a functional separation undertaking  Schedule 2  Local access lines  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020 No. 47, 2020  that relates to local access line services supplied, or proposed to be supplied, using the line; the person must not, on or after the designated commencement date, discriminate in favour of itself in relation to the supply of the eligible service. Ancillary contraventions" ;
    skos:definition "(4) If:  (a) a person supplies, or proposes to supply, an eligible service using a local access line:  (i) to itself; and  (ii) to its wholesale customers or prospective wholesale customers; and  (b) any of the following conditions is satisfied:  (i) section 142C applies to the line;  (ii) section 143 applies to the line;  (iii) neither section 142C nor section 143 applies to the line, and there is in force a functional separation undertaking  Schedule 2  Local access lines  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020 No. 47, 2020  that relates to local access line services supplied, or proposed to be supplied, using the line; the person must not, on or after the designated commencement date, discriminate in favour of itself in relation to the supply of the eligible service. Ancillary contraventions"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "30514ca09ec034924190ec25755b7a8a5147de8fea4567783e26943d4b5d1b52" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zf ;
    cof:pageNumber "80"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Discrimination in favor of itself is prohibited on or after the designated commencement date." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
