doc:sch-2-sec-161-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "161(4) Extended meaning of residential customer" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) For the purposes of this Part, if a business is carried on by a trust, and:  (a) most or all of the work of the business is carried out at the residence of an individual who is:  (i) a trustee of the trust; or  (ii) the director, or one of the directors, of a corporation that is a trustee of the trust; or  (b) the business does not occupy any premises other than the residence of an individual who is:  (i) a trustee of the trust; or  (ii) the director, or one of the directors, of a corporation that is a trustee of the trust; a trustee of the trust, in the trustee’s capacity as a customer, is taken to be a residential customer.  Schedule 2  Local access lines  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020 No. 47, 2020" ;
    cof:pageNumber "100"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-162 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "162 Close proximity"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-162 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if specified circumstances exist in relation to premises and a line, the premises are taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be in close proximity to the line.  (2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if specified circumstances exist in relation to premises and a line, the premises are taken, for the purposes of this Part, not to be in close proximity to the line.  (3) A determination under subsection (1) or (2) must be of a legislative character. Delegation to the ACCC  (4) The Minister may, by writing, delegate to the ACCC any or all of the Minister’s powers under the following provisions:  (a) subsection (1);  (b) subsection (2).  (5) In performing a delegated function or exercising a delegated power, the ACCC must comply with any written directions of the Minister." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if specified circumstances exist in relation to premises and a line, the premises are taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be in close proximity to the line.  (2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if specified circumstances exist in relation to premises and a line, the premises are taken, for the purposes of this Part, not to be in close proximity to the line.  (3) A determination under subsection (1) or (2) must be of a legislative character. Delegation to the ACCC  (4) The Minister may, by writing, delegate to the ACCC any or all of the Minister’s powers under the following provisions:  (a) subsection (1);  (b) subsection (2).  (5) In performing a delegated function or exercising a delegated power, the ACCC must comply with any written directions of the Minister."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f763c47d7be612f644209eadf369acb335be6a0f9863ab3762901dc613ff780d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "102"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-162-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-162-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-162-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-162-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-162-ss-5 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.102" .
doc:sch-2-sec-162 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "162 Close proximity" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if specified circumstances exist in relation to premises and a line, the premises are taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be in close proximity to the line.  (2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if specified circumstances exist in relation to premises and a line, the premises are taken, for the purposes of this Part, not to be in close proximity to the line.  (3) A determination under subsection (1) or (2) must be of a legislative character. Delegation to the ACCC  (4) The Minister may, by writing, delegate to the ACCC any or all of the Minister’s powers under the following provisions:  (a) subsection (1);  (b) subsection (2).  (5) In performing a delegated function or exercising a delegated power, the ACCC must comply with any written directions of the Minister." ;
    cof:pageNumber "102"^^xsd:integer .

