concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-80a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "80A After subsection 564(3)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-80a ;
    values:originalText "Insert: Injunctions relating to contraventions of section 151ZI  (3AA) If a person has engaged, is engaging or is proposing to engage, in any conduct in contravention of section 151ZI, the Federal Court may, on the application of a carrier or a carriage service provider, grant an injunction:  (a) restraining the person from engaging in the conduct; and  (b) if, in the court’s opinion, it is desirable to do so—requiring the person to do something.  (3AB) Subsection (3AA) does not, by implication, limit subsection (1)." ;
    skos:definition "Insert: Injunctions relating to contraventions of section 151ZI  (3AA) If a person has engaged, is engaging or is proposing to engage, in any conduct in contravention of section 151ZI, the Federal Court may, on the application of a carrier or a carriage service provider, grant an injunction:  (a) restraining the person from engaging in the conduct; and  (b) if, in the court’s opinion, it is desirable to do so—requiring the person to do something.  (3AB) Subsection (3AA) does not, by implication, limit subsection (1)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d4e991f3bb53c4b6efd19e9df5a1a888fbb593a83c4532e78af56f5711995553" ;
    cof:pageNumber "103"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Granting injunctions for contraventions of section 151ZI" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
