doc:sch-3-sec-360 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "360 Simplified outline of this Part" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "• The statutory infrastructure provider for a service area must, on reasonable request by a carriage service provider on behalf of an end-user at premises in the service area, connect the premises to a qualifying telecommunications network in order that the carriage service provider can provide qualifying carriage services to the end-user at the premises. • A statutory infrastructure provider must comply with standards, benchmarks and rules determined by the Minister. • A statutory infrastructure provider must publish the terms and conditions on which it offers to:  (a) connect premises; or  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3 Amendments  Part 1  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (b) supply related eligible services to carriage service providers." ;
    cof:pageNumber "108"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "360A Definitions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-360a ;
    values:originalText "In this Part: access agreement has the same meaning as in Part XIC of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010. building redevelopment project has the meaning given by section 360Y. designated day means the day on which a declaration is made under paragraph 48(1)(c) or (2)(a) of the National Broadband Network Companies Act 2011. Note: The declaration will state that, in the Minister’s opinion, the national broadband network should be treated as built and fully operational. designated service area has the meaning given by section 360L. eligible service has the same meaning as in section 152AL of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010. GDA94 means Geocentric Datum of Australia 1994. general service area has the meaning given by section 360F. interim NBN service area has the meaning given by section 360D. NBN Co has the same meaning as in the National Broadband Network Companies Act 2011. nominated service area has the meaning given by section 360H or 360J. project area, for a building redevelopment project, has the meaning given by section 360Y. provisional interim NBN service area has the meaning given by section 360D.  Schedule 3  Statutory infrastructure providers etc." ;
    skos:definition "In this Part: access agreement has the same meaning as in Part XIC of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010. building redevelopment project has the meaning given by section 360Y. designated day means the day on which a declaration is made under paragraph 48(1)(c) or (2)(a) of the National Broadband Network Companies Act 2011. Note: The declaration will state that, in the Minister’s opinion, the national broadband network should be treated as built and fully operational. designated service area has the meaning given by section 360L. eligible service has the same meaning as in section 152AL of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010. GDA94 means Geocentric Datum of Australia 1994. general service area has the meaning given by section 360F. interim NBN service area has the meaning given by section 360D. NBN Co has the same meaning as in the National Broadband Network Companies Act 2011. nominated service area has the meaning given by section 360H or 360J. project area, for a building redevelopment project, has the meaning given by section 360Y. provisional interim NBN service area has the meaning given by section 360D.  Schedule 3  Statutory infrastructure providers etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6a59c57c63276f21d31d940ddaf79a7abfb78d875baeba7c60a4a733df2cadca" ;
    cof:pageNumber "109"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Definitions for Schedule 3" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
