concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360ha a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "360HA Nominated service area—anticipatory notice to be given to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-360ha ;
    values:originalText "the ACMA by a carrier Nominated service area—real estate development project  (1) If:  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3 Amendments  Part 1  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (a) after the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than an NBN corporation) enters into a contract for the installation of telecommunications network infrastructure that will enable the supply of eligible services to premises in the whole of the project area of a real estate development project; and  (b) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be required, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole of the project area is a provisional nominated service area for the purposes of this Part; the carrier must:  (c) give the ACMA a written notice that:  (i) states that the carrier has entered into the contract; and  (ii) specifies the project area; and  (iii) describes the telecommunications network infrastructure that is to be installed under the contract; and  (iv) sets out the carrier’s estimate of the likely completion date for the installation; and  (d) do so within 10 business days after entering into the contract. Note: For the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA.  (2) If:  (a) before the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than an NBN corporation) entered into a contract for the installation of telecommunications network infrastructure that will enable the supply of eligible services to premises in the whole of the project area of a real estate development project; and  (b) the installation was not completed before the commencement of this section; and  (c) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be required, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole of the project area is a provisional nominated service area for the purposes of this Part; the carrier must:  (d) give the ACMA a written notice that:  (i) states that the carrier has entered into the contract; and  (ii) specifies the project area; and  Schedule 3  Statutory infrastructure providers etc." ;
    skos:definition "the ACMA by a carrier Nominated service area—real estate development project  (1) If:  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3 Amendments  Part 1  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (a) after the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than an NBN corporation) enters into a contract for the installation of telecommunications network infrastructure that will enable the supply of eligible services to premises in the whole of the project area of a real estate development project; and  (b) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be required, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole of the project area is a provisional nominated service area for the purposes of this Part; the carrier must:  (c) give the ACMA a written notice that:  (i) states that the carrier has entered into the contract; and  (ii) specifies the project area; and  (iii) describes the telecommunications network infrastructure that is to be installed under the contract; and  (iv) sets out the carrier’s estimate of the likely completion date for the installation; and  (d) do so within 10 business days after entering into the contract. Note: For the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA.  (2) If:  (a) before the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than an NBN corporation) entered into a contract for the installation of telecommunications network infrastructure that will enable the supply of eligible services to premises in the whole of the project area of a real estate development project; and  (b) the installation was not completed before the commencement of this section; and  (c) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be required, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole of the project area is a provisional nominated service area for the purposes of this Part; the carrier must:  (d) give the ACMA a written notice that:  (i) states that the carrier has entered"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a30af39301583857043816c9bb7b61bc491cc85fbf1ba2a773547b00ed3a962e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "120"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360ha-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360ha-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.120" .
doc:sch-3-sec-360ha a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "360HA Nominated service area—anticipatory notice to be given to" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "the ACMA by a carrier Nominated service area—real estate development project  (1) If:  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3 Amendments  Part 1  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (a) after the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than an NBN corporation) enters into a contract for the installation of telecommunications network infrastructure that will enable the supply of eligible services to premises in the whole of the project area of a real estate development project; and  (b) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be required, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole of the project area is a provisional nominated service area for the purposes of this Part; the carrier must:  (c) give the ACMA a written notice that:  (i) states that the carrier has entered into the contract; and  (ii) specifies the project area; and  (iii) describes the telecommunications network infrastructure that is to be installed under the contract; and  (iv) sets out the carrier’s estimate of the likely completion date for the installation; and  (d) do so within 10 business days after entering into the contract. Note: For the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA.  (2) If:  (a) before the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than an NBN corporation) entered into a contract for the installation of telecommunications network infrastructure that will enable the supply of eligible services to premises in the whole of the project area of a real estate development project; and  (b) the installation was not completed before the commencement of this section; and  (c) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be required, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole of the project area is a provisional nominated service area for the purposes of this Part; the carrier must:  (d) give the ACMA a written notice that:  (i) states that the carrier has entered into the contract; and  (ii) specifies the project area; and  Schedule 3  Statutory infrastructure providers etc." ;
    cof:pageNumber "120"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360ha-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "360HA(1) Nominated service area—anticipatory notice to be given to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-360ha-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3 Amendments  Part 1  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (a) after the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than an NBN corporation) enters into a contract for the installation of telecommunications network infrastructure that will enable the supply of eligible services to premises in the whole of the project area of a real estate development project; and  (b) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be required, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole of the project area is a provisional nominated service area for the purposes of this Part; the carrier must:  (c) give the ACMA a written notice that:  (i) states that the carrier has entered into the contract; and  (ii) specifies the project area; and  (iii) describes the telecommunications network infrastructure that is to be installed under the contract; and  (iv) sets out the carrier’s estimate of the likely completion date for the installation; and  (d) do so within 10 business days after entering into the contract. Note: For the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3 Amendments  Part 1  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (a) after the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than an NBN corporation) enters into a contract for the installation of telecommunications network infrastructure that will enable the supply of eligible services to premises in the whole of the project area of a real estate development project; and  (b) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be required, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole of the project area is a provisional nominated service area for the purposes of this Part; the carrier must:  (c) give the ACMA a written notice that:  (i) states that the carrier has entered into the contract; and  (ii) specifies the project area; and  (iii) describes the telecommunications network infrastructure that is to be installed under the contract; and  (iv) sets out the carrier’s estimate of the likely completion date for the installation; and  (d) do so within 10 business days after entering into the contract. Note: For the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "70bbaba2f37b98a5a1f536bcc928b034e46d4943c3aa46fc7487493a924440b3" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360ha ;
    cof:pageNumber "120"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Carrier must give ACMA written notice within 10 business days after entering into contract for installation of telecommunications network infrastructure." ;
    dc:description "written notice stating that carrier has entered into the contract, specifying project area and telecommunications network infrastructure to be installed" ;
