concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360q a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "360Q Obligation of statutory infrastructure provider to supply"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-360q ;
    values:originalText "eligible services—premises  (1) The statutory infrastructure provider for a service area must, on reasonable request by a carriage service provider:  (a) supply an eligible service to the carriage service provider in order that the carriage service provider can provide qualifying carriage services to end-users at premises in the service area; and  (b) do so on the terms and conditions that were published on the statutory infrastructure provider’s website at the time when the request was made. Note: For publication, see section 360X.  (1A) The eligible service must enable the carriage service provider to supply, to end-users at premises in the service area, carriage  Schedule 3  Statutory infrastructure providers etc." ;
    skos:definition "eligible services—premises  (1) The statutory infrastructure provider for a service area must, on reasonable request by a carriage service provider:  (a) supply an eligible service to the carriage service provider in order that the carriage service provider can provide qualifying carriage services to end-users at premises in the service area; and  (b) do so on the terms and conditions that were published on the statutory infrastructure provider’s website at the time when the request was made. Note: For publication, see section 360X.  (1A) The eligible service must enable the carriage service provider to supply, to end-users at premises in the service area, carriage  Schedule 3  Statutory infrastructure providers etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9787a80d14de3beddd6d971b9d6a7968e7ac338e02b1349eca9e04baabb0c415" ;
    cof:pageNumber "129"^^xsd:integer ;
