concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360r a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "360R Notification obligations of statutory infrastructure provider"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-360r ;
    values:originalText "Scope  (1) This section applies if a carrier (the first carrier) is the statutory infrastructure provider for:  (a) a nominated service area; or  (b) a designated service area. Obligations  (2) If the first carrier becomes aware that it is likely that it will no longer be able to fulfil its obligations under section 360P or 360Q, so far as they relate to the area, the first carrier must:  (a) give written notice of the matter to:  (i) the Secretary of the Department; and  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3 Amendments  Part 1  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (ii) the ACMA; and  (b) do so as soon as practicable after becoming so aware.  (3) If:  (a) subsection (2) applies; and  (b) the first carrier becomes aware that another carrier is willing to become the statutory infrastructure provider for the area; the first carrier must:  (c) give written notice of the matter to:  (i) the Secretary of the Department; and  (ii) the ACMA; and  (d) do so as soon as practicable after becoming so aware." ;
    skos:definition "Scope  (1) This section applies if a carrier (the first carrier) is the statutory infrastructure provider for:  (a) a nominated service area; or  (b) a designated service area. Obligations  (2) If the first carrier becomes aware that it is likely that it will no longer be able to fulfil its obligations under section 360P or 360Q, so far as they relate to the area, the first carrier must:  (a) give written notice of the matter to:  (i) the Secretary of the Department; and  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3 Amendments  Part 1  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (ii) the ACMA; and  (b) do so as soon as practicable after becoming so aware.  (3) If:  (a) subsection (2) applies; and  (b) the first carrier becomes aware that another carrier is willing to become the statutory infrastructure provider for the area; the first carrier must:  (c) give written notice of the matter to:  (i) the Secretary of the Department; and  (ii) the ACMA; and  (d) do so as soon as practicable after becoming so aware."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000" ;
