concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360v-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "360V(3) Rules"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-360v-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) However, a statutory infrastructure provider is not required to comply with a rule under subsection (1) to the extent that the rule is inconsistent with an access agreement to which the statutory infrastructure provider is a party, so long as:  (a) the agreement was entered into before the commencement of the rule; and  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3 Amendments  Part 1  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (b) the agreement has not been varied after the commencement of the rule." ;
    skos:definition "(3) However, a statutory infrastructure provider is not required to comply with a rule under subsection (1) to the extent that the rule is inconsistent with an access agreement to which the statutory infrastructure provider is a party, so long as:  (a) the agreement was entered into before the commencement of the rule; and  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3 Amendments  Part 1  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (b) the agreement has not been varied after the commencement of the rule."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2936d1a68c217eda982f702d5c6a984c28701fa45eb9142f1ffb44ba59befd97" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360v ;
    cof:pageNumber "136"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Exemption from rule compliance for access agreements entered before rule commencement" ;
