concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360za a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "360ZA Delegation"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-360za ;
    values:originalText "Delegation to the ACMA  (1) The Minister may, by writing, delegate to the ACMA any or all of the Minister’s powers under the following provisions:  (a) subsection 360D(14);  (b) subsection 360H(3);  (c) subsection 360H(5);  (d) subsection 360H(7);  (e) subsection 360H(11);  (f) subsection 360P(3);  (g) subsection 360P(5);  (h) subsection 360P(10);  (i) subsection 360Q(4);  (j) subsection 360Q(6);  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3 Amendments  Part 1  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (k) subsection 360U(1);  (l) subsection 360U(6);  (m) subsection 360XA(1);  (n) subsection 360Y(3).  (2) In performing a delegated function or exercising a delegated power, the ACMA must comply with any written directions of the Minister. Delegation to a member of the ACMA or to a member of the staff of the ACMA  (3) The Minister may, by writing, delegate to:  (a) a member of the ACMA; or  (b) a person who is:  (i) a member of the staff of the ACMA; and  (ii) an SES employee or acting SES employee; any or all of the Minister’s powers under subsection 360H(14) (variation of nominated service area declaration).  (4) In exercising a delegated power, the delegate must comply with any written directions of the Minister.  Schedule 3  Statutory infrastructure providers etc." ;
    skos:definition "Delegation to the ACMA  (1) The Minister may, by writing, delegate to the ACMA any or all of the Minister’s powers under the following provisions:  (a) subsection 360D(14);  (b) subsection 360H(3);  (c) subsection 360H(5);  (d) subsection 360H(7);  (e) subsection 360H(11);  (f) subsection 360P(3);  (g) subsection 360P(5);  (h) subsection 360P(10);  (i) subsection 360Q(4);  (j) subsection 360Q(6);  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3 Amendments  Part 1  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (k) subsection 360U(1);  (l) subsection 360U(6);  (m) subsection 360XA(1);  (n) subsection 360Y(3).  (2) In performing a delegated function or exercising a delegated power, the ACMA must comply with any written directions of the Minister. Delegation to a member of the ACMA or to a member of the staff of the ACMA  (3) The Minister may, by writing, delegate to:  (a) a member of the ACMA; or  (b) a person who is:  (i) a member of the staff of the ACMA; and  (ii) an SES employee or acting SES employee; any or all of the Minister’s powers under subsection 360H(14) (variation of nominated service area declaration).  (4) In exercising a delegated power, the delegate must comply with any written directions of the Minister.  Schedule 3  Statutory infrastructure providers etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cb133d2cf6587c1d573ec7e96a7e81a04ed023581a0b99d5523cadab9b5f9015" ;
    cof:pageNumber "140"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360za-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360za-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360za-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360za-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.140" .
doc:sch-3-sec-360za a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "360ZA Delegation" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Delegation to the ACMA  (1) The Minister may, by writing, delegate to the ACMA any or all of the Minister’s powers under the following provisions:  (a) subsection 360D(14);  (b) subsection 360H(3);  (c) subsection 360H(5);  (d) subsection 360H(7);  (e) subsection 360H(11);  (f) subsection 360P(3);  (g) subsection 360P(5);  (h) subsection 360P(10);  (i) subsection 360Q(4);  (j) subsection 360Q(6);  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3 Amendments  Part 1  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (k) subsection 360U(1);  (l) subsection 360U(6);  (m) subsection 360XA(1);  (n) subsection 360Y(3).  (2) In performing a delegated function or exercising a delegated power, the ACMA must comply with any written directions of the Minister. Delegation to a member of the ACMA or to a member of the staff of the ACMA  (3) The Minister may, by writing, delegate to:  (a) a member of the ACMA; or  (b) a person who is:  (i) a member of the staff of the ACMA; and  (ii) an SES employee or acting SES employee; any or all of the Minister’s powers under subsection 360H(14) (variation of nominated service area declaration).  (4) In exercising a delegated power, the delegate must comply with any written directions of the Minister.  Schedule 3  Statutory infrastructure providers etc." ;
    cof:pageNumber "140"^^xsd:integer .

