    cof:title "82(10) Condition about compliance with Ministerial determination" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(10) Despite subsection (6), a determination under subsection (2) has no effect to the extent to which it specifies the price, or a method of ascertaining the price, for any of the services, facilities or customer  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Schedule 4  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  equipment to be supplied by the grant recipient of a section 80 grant in accordance with the terms and conditions of the grant." ;
    cof:pageNumber "157"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-83 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "83 Secretary has powers etc. of the Commonwealth"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-83 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Secretary, on behalf of the Commonwealth, has all the rights, responsibilities, duties and powers of the Commonwealth in relation to the Commonwealth’s capacity as:  (a) a party to a contract entered into under section 80; or  (b) the grantor of a grant made under section 80.  (2) Without limiting subsection (1):  (a) an amount payable by the Commonwealth under a section 80 contract is to be paid by the Secretary on behalf of the Commonwealth; and  (b) an amount payable to the Commonwealth under a section 80 contract is to be paid to the Secretary on behalf of the Commonwealth; and  (c) a section 80 grant is to be paid by the Secretary on behalf of the Commonwealth; and  (d) an amount payable to the Commonwealth by way of the repayment of the whole or a part of a section 80 grant is to be paid to the Secretary on behalf of the Commonwealth; and  (e) the Secretary may institute an action or proceeding on behalf of the Commonwealth in relation to a matter that concerns:  (i) a section 80 contract; or  (ii) a section 80 grant." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Secretary, on behalf of the Commonwealth, has all the rights, responsibilities, duties and powers of the Commonwealth in relation to the Commonwealth’s capacity as:  (a) a party to a contract entered into under section 80; or  (b) the grantor of a grant made under section 80.  (2) Without limiting subsection (1):  (a) an amount payable by the Commonwealth under a section 80 contract is to be paid by the Secretary on behalf of the Commonwealth; and  (b) an amount payable to the Commonwealth under a section 80 contract is to be paid to the Secretary on behalf of the Commonwealth; and  (c) a section 80 grant is to be paid by the Secretary on behalf of the Commonwealth; and  (d) an amount payable to the Commonwealth by way of the repayment of the whole or a part of a section 80 grant is to be paid to the Secretary on behalf of the Commonwealth; and  (e) the Secretary may institute an action or proceeding on behalf of the Commonwealth in relation to a matter that concerns:  (i) a section 80 contract; or  (ii) a section 80 grant."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6c6412361bf6c2f12ee4d8aa67332e7b793e0cb2018ffe284d09988d306a9f94" ;
    cof:pageNumber "159"^^xsd:integer ;
