doc:sch-4-sec-85-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "85(1) Monitoring of performance" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Secretary must monitor, and report each financial year to the Minister on, all significant matters relating to:  (a) the performance of contractors; and  Schedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020 No. 47, 2020  (b) the performance of grant recipients." ;
    cof:pageNumber "159"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-85-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "85(2) Monitoring of performance"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-85-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A report under subsection (1) for a financial year must set out details of the following matters:  (a) the adequacy of each contractor’s compliance, during that year, with the terms and conditions of a section 80 contract;  (b) the adequacy of each grant recipient’s compliance, during that year, with the terms and conditions of a section 80 grant;  (c) any notice of breach by a contractor of a section 80 contract, where the notice was given during that year;  (d) any notice of breach by a grant recipient of a term or condition of a section 80 grant, where the notice was given during that year;  (e) any remedial action taken by the Secretary during that year in response to a breach of a section 80 contract;  (f) any remedial action taken by the Secretary during that year in response to a breach of the terms or conditions of a section 80 grant;  (g) the result of any such remedial action." ;
    skos:definition "(2) A report under subsection (1) for a financial year must set out details of the following matters:  (a) the adequacy of each contractor’s compliance, during that year, with the terms and conditions of a section 80 contract;  (b) the adequacy of each grant recipient’s compliance, during that year, with the terms and conditions of a section 80 grant;  (c) any notice of breach by a contractor of a section 80 contract, where the notice was given during that year;  (d) any notice of breach by a grant recipient of a term or condition of a section 80 grant, where the notice was given during that year;  (e) any remedial action taken by the Secretary during that year in response to a breach of a section 80 contract;  (f) any remedial action taken by the Secretary during that year in response to a breach of the terms or conditions of a section 80 grant;  (g) the result of any such remedial action."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9632c4f3157ebb9db95323b81d75255a51d25935c4b61516aeda6d1fef98b27e" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-85 ;
    cof:pageNumber "159"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Report must provide details of contractor and grant recipient compliance, notices of breach, remedial actions, and their results." ;
    dc:description "Yes" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
