doc:sch-4-sec-96a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "96A Potentially concessional premises" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "For the purposes of this Part, if particular premises are potentially chargeable premises in relation to a person for a month because a carriage service provider (who may be the person) supplies a designated broadband service to:  (a) a residential customer who occupies the premises; or  (b) a small business customer who occupies the premises; the premises are potentially concessional premises in relation to the person for that month." ;
    cof:pageNumber "171"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-96b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "96B Recently connected greenfield premises"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-96b ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) during a period comprising the whole or a part of a month in an eligible financial year, a person is a carrier; and  (b) a declaration made under subsection 63(2) of the Telecommunications Act 1997 was in force on 30 June 2018 in relation to the carrier licence held by the person; and  Schedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020 No. 47, 2020  (c) the declaration provides that the person must (upon request by an end-user at relevant premises) connect, or arrange for another person on the person’s behalf to connect, premises located in a development area (however described) specified in the declaration to a telecommunications network owned by the person (as specified in the declaration); and  (d) the person, or another person on the person’s behalf:  (i) has connected one or more premises located in the development area to the telecommunications network; and  (ii) has done so before the end of 30 June 2019; and  (e) one or more of the connected premises are potentially chargeable premises in relation to the person for that month; each of the potentially chargeable premises mentioned in paragraph (e) are recently connected greenfield premises in relation to the person for that month.  (2) If:  (a) a person is a carrier; and  (b) during a period comprising the whole or a part of a month in an eligible financial year, the person supplies an eligible local bitstream access service using a local access line; and  (c) during a whole or a part of that period, a carriage service provider supplies a designated broadband service to one or more premises using the line; and  (d) one or more of those premises are potentially chargeable premises in relation to the person for that month; each of the potentially chargeable premises mentioned in paragraph (d) are recently connected greenfield premises in relation to the person for that month.  (3) In this section: eligible local bitstream access service means a local bitstream access service that is first supplied at a time during the period:  (a) beginning at the start of 1 January 2011; and  (b) ending at the end of 30 June 2019. local bitstream access service has the meaning given by a declaration that:  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Schedule 4  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (a) was made:  (i) under subsection 152AL(3) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010; and  (ii) in compliance with repealed subsection 152AL(3C) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010; and  (b) was in force immediately before the commencement of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) during a period comprising the whole or a part of a month in an eligible financial year, a person is a carrier; and  (b) a declaration made under subsection 63(2) of the Telecommunications Act 1997 was in force on 30 June 2018 in relation to the carrier licence held by the person; and  Schedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020 No. 47, 2020  (c) the declaration provides that the person must (upon request by an end-user at relevant premises) connect, or arrange for another person on the person’s behalf to connect, premises located in a development area (however described) specified in the declaration to a telecommunications network owned by the person (as specified in the declaration); and  (d) the person, or another person on the person’s behalf:  (i) has connected one or more premises located in the development area to the telecommunications network; and  (ii) has done so before the end of 30 June 2019; and  (e) one or more of the connected premises are potentially chargeable premises in relation to the person for that month; each of the potentially chargeable premises mentioned in paragraph (e) are recently connected greenfield premises in relation to the person for that month.  (2) If:  (a) a person is a carrier; and  (b) during a period comprising the whole or a part of a month in an eligible financial year, the person supplies an eligible local bitstream access service using a local access line; and  (c) during a whole or a part of that period, a carriage service provider supplies a designated broadband service to one or more premises using the line; and  (d) one or more of those premises are potentially chargeable premises in relation to the person for that month; each of the potentially chargeable premises mentioned in paragraph (d) are recently connected greenfield premises in relation to the person for that month.  (3) In this section: eli"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2d33a979d24a8ee89649d5f48317f091b2e768deeca5c9eb43f2f50e2bc90bd3" ;
    cof:pageNumber "171"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-96b-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-96b-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-96b-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.171" .
