    cml:premiseText "scheme is a subclass of another scheme" ;
    cml:conclusionText "another scheme is an upper bound of scheme" ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::dl" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-4-sec-97-ss-6 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "97(6) Anti-avoidance" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(6) For the purposes of this section, scheme means:  (a) any agreement, arrangement, understanding, promise or undertaking, whether express or implied; or  (b) any scheme, plan, proposal, action, course of action or course of conduct, whether unilateral or otherwise." ;
    cof:pageNumber "173"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "98 Charge offset certificate"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-98 ;
    values:originalText "Application  (1) If:  (a) a person is an eligible funding recipient; and  (b) the ACMA has made an assessment under section 102 setting out the charge payable by the person for a financial year (the charge financial year); the person may, at any time during the period:  (c) beginning when the assessment was made; and  (d) ending at the end of the standard due date (within the meaning of section 102D) for the charge financial year; apply to the Secretary for the issue to the person of a charge offset certificate for the charge financial year.  (2) An application under subsection (1) must:  (a) be in writing; and  (b) be in a form approved, in writing, by the Secretary; and  (c) be accompanied by such information as is specified in rules made under subsection (9).  Schedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020 No. 47, 2020  Issue of certificate  (3) If:  (a) an application under subsection (1) has been made for the issue to a person of a charge offset certificate for the charge financial year; and  (b) the person is the holder of a nominal funding entitlement certificate in relation to the next financial year; and  (c) rules made under subsection (9) for the purposes of this paragraph are in force; and  (d) the conditions set out in those rules are satisfied; the Secretary must:  (e) issue a certificate stating that the person is entitled to a charge offset for the charge financial year equal to the amount specified in the certificate; and  (f) do so by the end of 31 March next following the charge financial year.  (4) The amount specified in the certificate:  (a) must be the amount ascertained in accordance with rules made under subsection (9); and  (b) must not exceed the nominal funding entitlement of the person for the next financial year; and  (c) must not exceed the annual base amount of the person for the charge financial year.  (5) A certificate issued under subsection (3) is to be known as a charge offset certificate. Refusal  (6) If the Secretary decides to refuse to issue a charge offset certificate to a person, the Secretary must give written notice of the decision to the person. Copy of certificate  (7) If the Secretary issues a charge offset certificate, the Secretary must give a copy of the certificate to the ACMA.  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Schedule 4  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  Charge offset certificate cannot be transferred  (8) A charge offset certificate cannot be transferred. Rules  (9) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules for the purposes of this section." ;
    skos:definition "Application  (1) If:  (a) a person is an eligible funding recipient; and  (b) the ACMA has made an assessment under section 102 setting out the charge payable by the person for a financial year (the charge financial year); the person may, at any time during the period:  (c) beginning when the assessment was made; and  (d) ending at the end of the standard due date (within the meaning of section 102D) for the charge financial year; apply to the Secretary for the issue to the person of a charge offset certificate for the charge financial year.  (2) An application under subsection (1) must:  (a) be in writing; and  (b) be in a form approved, in writing, by the Secretary; and  (c) be accompanied by such information as is specified in rules made under subsection (9).  Schedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020 No. 47, 2020  Issue of certificate  (3) If:  (a) an application under subsection (1) has been made for the issue to a person of a charge offset certificate for the charge financial year; and  (b) the person is the holder of a nominal funding entitlement certificate in relation to the next financial year; and  (c) rules made under subsection (9) for the purposes of this paragraph are in force; and  (d) the conditions set out in those rules are satisfied; the Secretary must:  (e) issue a certificate stating that the person is entitled to a charge offset for the charge financial year equal to the amount specified in the certificate; and  (f) do so by the end of 31 March next following the charge financial year.  (4) The amount specified in the certificate:  (a) must be the amount ascertained in accordance with rules made under subsection (9); and  (b) must not exceed the nominal funding entitlement of the person for the next financial year; and  (c) must not exceed the annual base amount of the person for the charge financial year.  (5) A certificate issued under"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e7ad522ea327e5ba95534ef8355038ef7f7b86328c7cf9175886f60464c40d28" ;
    cof:pageNumber "175"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98-ss-5 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98-ss-6 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98-ss-7 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98-ss-8 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98-ss-9 ;
