concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-99 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "99 Remission or refund of charge"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-99 ;
    values:originalText "Remission  (1) If:  (a) a person becomes the holder of a charge offset certificate for a financial year; and  (b) a base instalment of charge is payable by the person in relation to the financial year; and  (c) the base instalment of charge has not been paid; the Secretary must, on behalf of the Commonwealth, remit so much of the base instalment of charge as equals the amount specified in the certificate. Note: For base instalment of charge, see section 102D.  (2) The Secretary must inform the ACMA of a remission of charge under subsection (1).  (3) If:  (a) the ACMA has made an assessment under section 102 setting out the charge payable by a person for a financial year; and  (b) the base instalment of charge is remitted, to any extent, under subsection (1) of this section; and  (c) the ACMA is informed of the remission; the ACMA must, under subsection 102B(1), vary the assessment to reflect the remission. Refund  (4) If:  Schedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020 No. 47, 2020  (a) a person becomes the holder of a charge offset certificate for a financial year; and  (b) a base instalment of charge was payable by the person in relation to the financial year; and  (c) the base instalment of charge has been paid; the Secretary must, on behalf of the Commonwealth, refund so much of the base instalment of charge as equals the amount specified in the certificate. Note: For base instalment of charge, see section 102D." ;
    skos:definition "Remission  (1) If:  (a) a person becomes the holder of a charge offset certificate for a financial year; and  (b) a base instalment of charge is payable by the person in relation to the financial year; and  (c) the base instalment of charge has not been paid; the Secretary must, on behalf of the Commonwealth, remit so much of the base instalment of charge as equals the amount specified in the certificate. Note: For base instalment of charge, see section 102D.  (2) The Secretary must inform the ACMA of a remission of charge under subsection (1).  (3) If:  (a) the ACMA has made an assessment under section 102 setting out the charge payable by a person for a financial year; and  (b) the base instalment of charge is remitted, to any extent, under subsection (1) of this section; and  (c) the ACMA is informed of the remission; the ACMA must, under subsection 102B(1), vary the assessment to reflect the remission. Refund  (4) If:  Schedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020 No. 47, 2020  (a) a person becomes the holder of a charge offset certificate for a financial year; and  (b) a base instalment of charge was payable by the person in relation to the financial year; and  (c) the base instalment of charge has been paid; the Secretary must, on behalf of the Commonwealth, refund so much of the base instalment of charge as equals the amount specified in the certificate. Note: For base instalment of charge, see section 102D."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "13d493e3219ca27150a7aa4096c4746b31725c5bacd3f994115cc0898e6674fc" ;
    cof:pageNumber "177"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-99-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-99-ss-2 ;
