concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-99-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "99(3) Remission or refund of charge"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-99-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If:  (a) the ACMA has made an assessment under section 102 setting out the charge payable by a person for a financial year; and  (b) the base instalment of charge is remitted, to any extent, under subsection (1) of this section; and  (c) the ACMA is informed of the remission; the ACMA must, under subsection 102B(1), vary the assessment to reflect the remission. Refund" ;
    skos:definition "(3) If:  (a) the ACMA has made an assessment under section 102 setting out the charge payable by a person for a financial year; and  (b) the base instalment of charge is remitted, to any extent, under subsection (1) of this section; and  (c) the ACMA is informed of the remission; the ACMA must, under subsection 102B(1), vary the assessment to reflect the remission. Refund"@en ;
