concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102n a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "102N Late payment penalty"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-102n ;
    values:originalText "(1) If an amount of:  (a) charge; or  (b) an instalment of charge; that is payable by a person remains unpaid after the day on which it becomes due and payable, the person is liable to pay a penalty (late payment penalty) on the unpaid amount for each day until all of:  (c) the charge; or  (d) the instalment of charge; as the case may be, has been paid.  (2) The late payment penalty rate is 20% per year, or such lower rate as the ACMA determines in writing for the purposes of this subsection.  (3) The ACMA may remit the whole or part of a late payment penalty that a person is liable to pay under subsection (1).  (4) The late payment penalty for a day is due and payable at the end of that day.  (5) Late payment penalty:  (a) is a debt due to the ACMA on behalf of the Commonwealth; and  (b) may be recovered by the ACMA, on behalf of the Commonwealth, in:  (i) the Federal Court; or  (ii) the Federal Circuit Court; or  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Schedule 4  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (iii) a court of a State or Territory that has jurisdiction in relation to the matter.  (6) If the amount of the late payment penalty for a day is not an amount of whole dollars, the late payment penalty is rounded to the nearest dollar (rounding 50 cents upwards).  (7) A determination under subsection (2) is a legislative instrument." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If an amount of:  (a) charge; or  (b) an instalment of charge; that is payable by a person remains unpaid after the day on which it becomes due and payable, the person is liable to pay a penalty (late payment penalty) on the unpaid amount for each day until all of:  (c) the charge; or  (d) the instalment of charge; as the case may be, has been paid.  (2) The late payment penalty rate is 20% per year, or such lower rate as the ACMA determines in writing for the purposes of this subsection.  (3) The ACMA may remit the whole or part of a late payment penalty that a person is liable to pay under subsection (1).  (4) The late payment penalty for a day is due and payable at the end of that day.  (5) Late payment penalty:  (a) is a debt due to the ACMA on behalf of the Commonwealth; and  (b) may be recovered by the ACMA, on behalf of the Commonwealth, in:  (i) the Federal Court; or  (ii) the Federal Circuit Court; or  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Schedule 4  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (iii) a court of a State or Territory that has jurisdiction in relation to the matter.  (6) If the amount of the late payment penalty for a day is not an amount of whole dollars, the late payment penalty is rounded to the nearest dollar (rounding 50 cents upwards).  (7) A determination under subsection (2) is a legislative instrument."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5a34cca8715562ece4208bd67bd91479cbc7c64e51bcd7de678934eb862972d3" ;
    cof:pageNumber "188"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102n-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102n-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102n-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102n-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102n-ss-5 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102n-ss-6 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102n-ss-7 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
