concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102s a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "102S ACMA may retain documents"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-102s ;
    values:originalText "(1) The ACMA may take, and retain for as long as is necessary, possession of a document produced under subsection 102P(2).  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Schedule 4  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (2) The carrier or carriage service provider otherwise entitled to possession of the document is entitled to be supplied, as soon as practicable, with a copy certified by the ACMA to be a true copy.  (3) The certified copy must be received in all courts and tribunals as evidence as if it were the original.  (4) Until a certified copy is supplied, the ACMA must, at such times and places as the ACMA thinks appropriate, permit the carrier or carriage service provider otherwise entitled to possession of the document, or a person authorised by that carrier or carriage service provider, to inspect and make copies of, or take extracts from, the document." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The ACMA may take, and retain for as long as is necessary, possession of a document produced under subsection 102P(2).  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Schedule 4  No. 47, 2020 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020  (2) The carrier or carriage service provider otherwise entitled to possession of the document is entitled to be supplied, as soon as practicable, with a copy certified by the ACMA to be a true copy.  (3) The certified copy must be received in all courts and tribunals as evidence as if it were the original.  (4) Until a certified copy is supplied, the ACMA must, at such times and places as the ACMA thinks appropriate, permit the carrier or carriage service provider otherwise entitled to possession of the document, or a person authorised by that carrier or carriage service provider, to inspect and make copies of, or take extracts from, the document."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "77eeda6d8665ae78114b51733ba838f1a1f66ba98a675fc48d21050b49d1d1a1" ;
    cof:pageNumber "190"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102s-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102s-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102s-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102s-ss-4 ;
