    cof:title "1(3A) July 2019 instead of the designated start date); and" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3A) If:  (a) notice of a motion to disallow the determination is given in a House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House after the copy of the determination was tabled in that House under section 38 of the Legislation Act 2003; and  (b) at the end of 15 sitting days of that House after the giving of that notice of motion:  (i) the notice has not been withdrawn and the motion has not been called on; or  (ii) the motion has been called on, moved and (where relevant) seconded and has not been withdrawn or otherwise disposed of; the determination is then taken to have been disallowed, and subsection (3) does not apply to the determination." ;
    cof:pageNumber "199"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-1-3-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "1(4) July 2019 instead of the designated start date); and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-1-3-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) Section 42 (disallowance) of the Legislation Act 2003 does not apply to the determination. Note 1: The 15 sitting day notice period mentioned in paragraph (2)(a) of this section is the same as the 15 sitting day notice period mentioned in paragraph 42(1)(a) of the Legislation Act 2003. Note 2: The 15 sitting day disallowance period mentioned in paragraph (2)(b) of this section is the same as the 15 sitting day disallowance period mentioned in paragraph 42(1)(b) of the Legislation Act 2003." ;
    skos:definition "(4) Section 42 (disallowance) of the Legislation Act 2003 does not apply to the determination. Note 1: The 15 sitting day notice period mentioned in paragraph (2)(a) of this section is the same as the 15 sitting day notice period mentioned in paragraph 42(1)(a) of the Legislation Act 2003. Note 2: The 15 sitting day disallowance period mentioned in paragraph (2)(b) of this section is the same as the 15 sitting day disallowance period mentioned in paragraph 42(1)(b) of the Legislation Act 2003."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5b55277d715110ac5bef2f2348a565dcf00e89e4760a41e677b7451ac8fb21eb" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-1-3 ;
    cof:pageNumber "199"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Minister may give the ACMA a written direction requiring the ACMA to make available specified information. Section 42 of the Legislation Act 2003 does not apply to the determination. Verification of statements in the report may be required." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
